title: 'B809 root cause: stale parent_task_id chain inflates subagent depth permanently'
updated_at: "2026-08-02T09:07:41Z"
---
Root cause identified: subagent_depth() walks the parent_task_id chain starting from find_task_id_by_session_key, which returns the most recent background task by id DESC regardless of status/age. For session telegram:58495225:58495225, old failed tasks (139->159->160->162) form a 4-level chain from months ago. Every new subagent spawn attempt hits depth>=4 and is rejected.\n\nFix: only count active (running/queued) tasks in the depth chain, or filter find_task_id_by_session_key to exclude completed/failed/cancelled tasks.